 omission matters given the acute need for comprehensive reproductive and sexual health care. Our support for access to that care around the world remains real and continuing. A survivor-centred approach cannot ignore this priority. These concerns do not alter our established commitment to survivor access to sexual and reproductive health care.\n\nThis post-vote statement does not establish endorsement of an unspecified future text or a future vote. It preserves our ongoing commitment while noting the defects in the adopted resolution.", "generated_tokens": 172, "generation_seconds": 4.282331265509129, "at_cap": false}
